    {
      "id": "AcVEZAmAyvFTDLg2fjIaK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2394.6602783203125,
      "y": -181,
      "width": 495.919677734375,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "as",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2061972026,
      "version": 443,
      "versionNonce": 48461222,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1752719385652,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. use notification_id for idempotency check\n2. store id in redis with a formed key and set\nexpiry of say 24 hours on the value\n3. This will ensure that we don't process the same\nnotification_id multiple times\n4. redis servers can be sharded using consistent\nhashing on the notification_id",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. use notification_id for idempotency check\n2. store id in redis with a formed key and set\nexpiry of say 24 hours on the value\n3. This will ensure that we don't process the same\nnotification_id multiple times\n4. redis servers can be sharded using consistent\nhashing on the notification_id",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "o1Ak2Zw-DQPtAMjrU5zi5",
